@prefix chorus: <https://jeffbridwell.com/chorus#> .
@prefix rdfs:   <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

# #4010 — Pulse's PRODUCT record, authored.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. ProductShape declares
# `chorus:instancesGraph "urn:chorus:instances"`, so /products reads the
# instances graph. The eight products served there (athena, borg, chorus,
# clearing, convergence, loom, pulse, werk) were LIVE-ONLY — materialized into
# the store in July, in no deployed file. Meanwhile
# designing/data/product-instances.ttl authors eight `product-*` records into
# urn:chorus:ontology, which /products never reads.
#
# That is why editing Pulse's design in product-instances.ttl deployed cleanly
# and changed nothing Jeff could see: the edit landed in the graph the API does
# not serve. Two records, two graphs, one of them invisible.
#
# This file makes the SERVED record the AUTHORED record. It is listed in
# platform/config/instance-seed-manifest.txt as `product:`, so
# `athena-model seed --deploy` writes it into urn:chorus:instances through the
# governed writer — the same per-subject additive merge every other instance
# group uses. An edit here now reaches /products/pulse and the products page.
#
# COMPLETE BY NECESSITY. The seed is a per-subject replace: every triple the
# live record carries is restated here, or it is dropped. The set below is the
# live record as measured 2026-08-27 06:10, with the four design fields
# (vision / valueProposition / audience / gaps) revised to current reality.
#
# rdfs:label and rdfs:comment are ADDED. ProductShape requires both
# (sh:minCount 1) and the live record carried neither — all eight served
# products are shape-invalid on those two paths today. Dual emission
# (rdfs: + chorus:) follows product-instances.ttl's own convention.
#
# The remaining seven products stay live-only. They are the same landmine and
# want the same treatment; that is not this card.

chorus:pulse a chorus:Product ;
    rdfs:label   "Pulse" ;
    chorus:label "Pulse" ;
    rdfs:comment   "Agent vital signs — heartbeats, declared role states, andon, at-a-glance health of the running team. Child product of The Clearing." ;
    chorus:comment "Agent vital signs — heartbeats, declared role states, andon, at-a-glance health of the running team. Child product of The Clearing." ;

    chorus:ownedBy chorus:role-wren ;
    chorus:status  "operating" ;
    chorus:atStep  chorus:value-stream-step-directing ;
    chorus:partOf  chorus:chorus ;
    chorus:publishesPreAuth "true" ;

    chorus:hasDomain chorus:memory ;
    chorus:hasDomain chorus:knowledge ;
    chorus:hasDomain chorus:search ;

    chorus:consumes chorus:events ;
    chorus:consumes chorus:streams ;
    chorus:consumes chorus:messages ;
    chorus:consumes chorus:memory ;
    chorus:consumes chorus:alerts-monitors ;

    chorus:hasDesignDoc chorus:document-pulse-service-design ;

    dcterms:created  "2026-07-09T16:03:08Z" ;
    dcterms:creator  "wren" ;
    dcterms:modified "2026-08-27T10:10:00Z" ;

    chorus:vision "The running team is legible at a glance — who is alive, building, blocked, or dark — without anyone asking. Jeff should never be the first to notice a stall, and no role should have to send a message to find out whether another role is working." ;

    chorus:valueProposition "Pulse is a read projection over the streams the team already emits: the spine, messages, alerts. Its promise is that silence becomes a signal. Its current implementation does not keep that promise — the state field is composed from what a role DECLARED, not from what the spine OBSERVED (platform/pulse/src/pulse.rs:162), so a role that is building but forgot to declare reads as idle. 142 cards have added new ways to declare. The fix is one derivation from the spine, with declared state demoted to a hint that loses to observation." ;

    chorus:audience "Jeff, at a glance, as the primary reader. The three roles, for mutual observation without asking each other. Alerting, as a downstream consumer." ;

    chorus:gaps "Measured 2026-08-27. (1) The state field is wrong by construction: pulse.rs:162 composes declared state; `inferred_stale: true` is the system knowing its own answer is wrong and having no authority to override it. Observed live 2026-08-25: kade read `idle` while running the nightly. (2) One of eight in-scope items from #2442 shipped — pulse-latest.json still has no schema_version and no sources. (3) Pulse models SUBJECTS (roles, cards, services) and no RELATIONS: it cannot answer who is waiting on whom, which is the question that actually costs Jeff time. (4) Until #4010, Pulse's own product record was live-only and unauthored, so this text could not be edited reproducibly — the defect that hid the three above." .
